00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:11.180
So you want to know what
the up-or-out principle

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:14.270
in consulting is and how it really works.

00:00:14.270 --> 00:00:18.010
So for sure, when I was a young
student, about 10 years ago

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:21.060
this was always a thing that
really gave me headaches.

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:23.660
When I was thinking about
maybe joining consulting

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:26.570
after graduation, what
does up-or-out really mean?

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:27.940
How does it work?

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:29.930
Does this mean that I might lose my job

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:32.010
if I do some mistakes on a project?

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:34.160
Will I just be kicked out of the firm

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:35.320
if I'm not good enough?

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:38.070
So for sure these were
questions which were in my head

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:41.048
and I didn't really have
any resources at the time

00:00:41.048 --> 00:00:42.810
to really understand this.

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:44.690
I always felt like this is a topic

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:46.210
that isn't really talked about

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:48.360
and for sure at some recruiting events

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:50.504
when I talked to representatives
of any of these firms

00:00:50.504 --> 00:00:52.970
I never really felt like
that I got a straight answer

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:55.200
that somebody was really spilling the tea

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.770
on what up-or-out really
means and how it works.

00:00:57.770 --> 00:01:00.120
So in this video, I'm
going to do exactly that

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:02.520
I'm going to talk about this little secret

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:04.100
of the consulting world.

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:05.630
So welcome to another coffee break

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:08.400
here on my channel Firm
Learning, my name is Heinrich

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.260
I'm a former McKinsey Consultant

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:12.527
and on my channel I want to
help you to become successful

00:01:12.527 --> 00:01:14.920
in the first years of your career.

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:15.910
So before we start

00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:18.450
I just wanna be clear that I'm not talking

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:21.080
about the situation of any specific firm

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:23.350
but rather talking about
the general situation

00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:24.837
of tier one consulting firms

00:01:24.837 --> 00:01:26.920
and I trust similar things will be true

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:29.060
for tier two and tier three firm as well.

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:30.550
It is also important to understand

00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:32.150
that within the same firm

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:35.170
how strict this up-or-out
principle is applied

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:36.502
might vary by geography

00:01:36.502 --> 00:01:38.900
also because of course the labor laws

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:40.700
a different country by country

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:42.660
with of course the residing implications

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:43.493
that come from that.

00:01:43.493 --> 00:01:45.990
So in this video I will
tackle the up-or-out principle

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:46.823
in three steps.

00:01:46.823 --> 00:01:47.833
First, I'm going to talk about

00:01:47.833 --> 00:01:50.090
what the up-or-out principal actually is.

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:51.440
What does this really mean?

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:52.910
Then second, I'm going to talk about

00:01:52.910 --> 00:01:55.040
how it really works in practice

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:56.650
and the third I'm going to talk about

00:01:56.650 --> 00:01:59.453
what happens if you are
on the out part, right?

00:01:59.453 --> 00:02:03.310
So if the firm asks you
decides that you cannot work

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:05.280
for the firm anymore in the future.

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:07.110
So without further ado, let's start

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:09.460
what does up-or-out even mean?

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:11.240
What is this even supposed to mean?

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:15.540
And indeed another word that
some people use is grow or go

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:17.633
and what this really boils
down to is that in the end

00:02:17.633 --> 00:02:19.807
throughout your career in consulting

00:02:19.807 --> 00:02:21.900
and you get either designated

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:24.380
either you get promoted to the next level

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:25.880
every other year or so

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:29.200
or at some point, if
you're not getting promoted

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:31.680
you will be asked to leave the firm.

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:34.640
So pretty much your work
contract will be terminated

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:36.780
you can assume that this
principle is applied

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:39.680
in a rather strict way
for all the MBB firms

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:40.810
and other tier one firms.

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:42.160
and again to some extent

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:43.990
also to tier two and tier three firms.

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:46.220
So then why do consulting firms do this?

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:48.210
What is their rationale for doing that?

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:51.610
Where they want to keep the
pyramid in the organization

00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:53.840
and they wanna make sure
that their credit system

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:56.070
where the very best get to the top

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:58.300
and the people who maybe do not perform

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:00.050
to these highest levels that they expect

00:03:00.050 --> 00:03:01.860
will at some point,
leave the organization.

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:03.960
This is exactly what
the up-or-out principal

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:05.580
is supposed to do so for our time

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:07.900
either you're good enough
for the next designation,

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:10.920
you're considered ready to
be promoted to the next level

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:12.170
or this is not a case.

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:13.247
You are not considered good enough

00:03:13.247 --> 00:03:15.520
and then you will need
to leave at some point.

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:18.310
But of course, there's also a
criticism for this principle

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:20.130
and maybe you're familiar
with the expression

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:22.249
of the Peter principle,
which pretty much means

00:03:22.249 --> 00:03:23.880
that in many organizations

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:26.770
people get always promoted up to the level

00:03:26.770 --> 00:03:28.620
of their personal incompetence.

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:32.160
So people might be very good,
highly effective in the jobs

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:35.110
that they used to do, but
then they always get promoted

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:36.950
up to a point that they failed

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:39.000
they cannot do this new role anymore

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:41.110
and then often this means
that you need to leave

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:42.460
the company as the employee.

00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:44.203
So if you translate this to consulting

00:03:44.203 --> 00:03:47.300
what this means is that maybe
you're a great project lead,

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:50.750
maybe you do an excellent
job at managing projects,

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:53.550
managing your clients, managing your team

00:03:53.550 --> 00:03:56.100
but maybe you just do not want to advance

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:59.020
into the junior partner
position as a next step

00:03:59.020 --> 00:04:01.012
maybe because you don't
want the lifestyle,

00:04:01.012 --> 00:04:04.220
you don't enjoy the tasks that
you will likely need to do.

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:06.540
So you would be very happy just to stay

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:09.130
in your project, lead role forever

00:04:09.130 --> 00:04:10.970
this is just what you're comfortable with

00:04:10.970 --> 00:04:12.220
this is what you enjoy doing,

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:14.720
this is also where you're really good at

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:18.440
and choices like this
are usually not possible

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:21.660
in these large strategy consulting firms

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:23.560
where the up-or-out principle applies.

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:27.680
So over time you either need
to go up or you need to go out

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:30.170
this is really what this boils down to.

00:04:30.170 --> 00:04:31.960
So let's now move to the second part

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:33.880
how does this really work?

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:36.570
How is this principle
really applied in practice?

