00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:03.080
and indeed would, most of
these consulting firms have

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:06.520
is that they have very highly
standardized careers tricks.

00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:08.953
So if you joined these firms,
you already know from day one

00:06:08.953 --> 00:06:11.660
that in one year he will
be promoted to this level

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:12.930
then in another year on average

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:14.430
you be promoted to the next level

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:16.560
then in two years to this level and so on

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:18.380
that you have an average time span

00:06:18.380 --> 00:06:20.900
until you pretty much know
that this is your career track

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:23.440
that you can follow to
get partner at some point

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:25.640
of course, for each of these steps

00:06:25.640 --> 00:06:27.490
there is some level of flexibility

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:29.740
and often this is described as a window.

00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:32.010
So you have often a certain time window

00:06:32.010 --> 00:06:35.080
with then you can make the
designation to the next step.

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:37.380
What is then means is
that in this time window

00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:39.273
usually there are three points in time

00:06:39.273 --> 00:06:41.070
that you can make the designation.

00:06:41.070 --> 00:06:42.700
So if you are considered a high performer,

00:06:42.700 --> 00:06:44.240
if you're considered a rock star

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:46.210
then you might have the
chance of being promoted

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:47.350
early in this window.

00:06:47.350 --> 00:06:48.810
So earlier than your peers

00:06:48.810 --> 00:06:51.840
and indeed often this difference
is only a couple of months

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:54.540
but if you are really one
of these high-performance

00:06:54.540 --> 00:06:58.500
who always consistently is
able to get promoted early.

00:06:58.500 --> 00:06:59.850
This really can add up

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:01.730
and then in the long-term
you might be able

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:04.440
to make partner one or
two or three years earlier

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:06.900
then there's the standard
regular point in time

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:10.003
where most people say
80% of all the people

00:07:10.003 --> 00:07:11.170
will get designated.

00:07:11.170 --> 00:07:13.190
So this is kind of the
average career track

00:07:13.190 --> 00:07:14.060
that you will be on

00:07:14.060 --> 00:07:17.050
and then there's also this late promotion,

00:07:17.050 --> 00:07:19.420
the late designation, and
this is for the people

00:07:19.420 --> 00:07:23.030
where for whatever reason,
the we're not yet seem fit

00:07:23.030 --> 00:07:26.730
to be designated in the
standard regular point in time.

00:07:26.730 --> 00:07:29.291
Maybe they've got some subpar
performance evaluations,

00:07:29.291 --> 00:07:32.120
maybe there were some
things in their development

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:33.950
where some partners expressed the opinion

00:07:33.950 --> 00:07:35.957
they still need to develop a certain area,

00:07:35.957 --> 00:07:38.050
a certain aspect of their skillset

00:07:38.050 --> 00:07:40.210
in order to be ready to
take on that new role

00:07:40.210 --> 00:07:42.750
to take on this new
responsibility that comes

00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:44.090
with the promotion attached to it

00:07:44.090 --> 00:07:47.306
and then indeed, a few are
designated in this late spot

00:07:47.306 --> 00:07:49.750
then you're fine, then you're designated

00:07:49.750 --> 00:07:51.250
and then your journey continues.

00:07:51.250 --> 00:07:53.300
and then maybe you have
another year or two

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:55.090
until the next window opens

00:07:55.090 --> 00:07:57.100
and this gives them plenty of opportunity

00:07:57.100 --> 00:07:59.480
to recalibrate also your
performance ratings.

00:07:59.480 --> 00:08:01.830
But then of course what can happen is that

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:03.087
then within this window

00:08:03.087 --> 00:08:06.630
there are people that
then do not get designated

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:08.250
and while on the more junior levels

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:10.990
its the big majority of
people get designated

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:13.460
as only a minority who
doesn't make this cut in.

00:08:13.460 --> 00:08:15.980
The more senior you get
up to the partner level,

00:08:15.980 --> 00:08:17.100
of course at some point,

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:18.880
the larger of the share of the people

00:08:18.880 --> 00:08:21.880
who does not make it will
need to leave the firm

00:08:21.880 --> 00:08:22.810
at some point in time.

00:08:22.810 --> 00:08:24.470
Of course, what we need to understand here

00:08:24.470 --> 00:08:27.770
is that these things do
not come by surprise.

00:08:27.770 --> 00:08:29.780
You would have received several instances

00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:31.540
of performance reviews before,

00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:34.539
you will not be surprised
that this is then the result

00:08:34.539 --> 00:08:38.240
if it really gets that far
this really happens to you

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:39.130
in the very end

00:08:39.130 --> 00:08:40.870
and in the moment we're
also going to talk about

00:08:40.870 --> 00:08:44.240
what really happens if you
are asked to leave the firm

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:45.790
or this process really looks like.

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:47.350
So stick with me here for a moment

00:08:47.350 --> 00:08:49.610
but again, it does not come as a surprise.

00:08:49.610 --> 00:08:51.770
It is a very transparent process

00:08:51.770 --> 00:08:53.930
and of course the consulting
firm that you work for

00:08:53.930 --> 00:08:55.800
usually wants you to succeed.

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:57.910
They already invested
lots of time and money

00:08:57.910 --> 00:08:59.250
just to hire you

00:08:59.250 --> 00:09:02.100
and already invested lots
of time into your training.

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:03.660
So they want you to succeed,

00:09:03.660 --> 00:09:05.850
so often the different processes starting

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:07.650
of somebody starting to fall behind

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:08.970
where you will get coaching,

00:09:08.970 --> 00:09:10.600
where you will get additional support

00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:12.290
and then this does enable lots of people

00:09:12.290 --> 00:09:14.030
to indeed improve their performance

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:15.800
and the make the cut to not in the end

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:18.280
be in this position where it
just doesn't work out anymore.

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:19.280
But then of course

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:21.920
every year people are
affected by up-or-out

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:23.610
people need to leave

00:09:23.610 --> 00:09:25.440
then the question is, how does this work?

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:27.000
What does this really mean?

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:28.716
And this is now the
third part of this video

00:09:28.716 --> 00:09:31.050
so what happens if you need to go?

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:32.910
And the other question
that I get most often

00:09:32.910 --> 00:09:34.670
if I discuss this topic with other people

00:09:34.670 --> 00:09:37.346
is that they say wait but
they cannot just fire you

00:09:37.346 --> 00:09:40.810
there are labor laws there, right?

00:09:40.810 --> 00:09:43.130
And of course this is a sensitive topic

00:09:43.130 --> 00:09:44.270
for the consulting firms.

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:46.471
Everybody has a big interest
of not letting this escalate

00:09:46.471 --> 00:09:48.640
to some legal type of situation.

00:09:48.640 --> 00:09:51.140
So what usually happens is
that the consulting firm

00:09:51.140 --> 00:09:51.973
will approach you,

00:09:51.973 --> 00:09:54.113
will just try to work
something out with you

00:09:54.113 --> 00:09:56.613
so that you can leave on
good terms and all of this

00:09:56.613 --> 00:09:58.420
is handled in an amicable way.

00:09:58.420 --> 00:09:59.660
So what this usually means

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:02.090
is that you will get
several months of time

00:10:02.090 --> 00:10:03.600
now to reorient yourself,

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:05.640
for this time you might
also get a paid leave

00:10:05.640 --> 00:10:07.430
so that you still receive the salary,

00:10:07.430 --> 00:10:10.330
but can again maybe do some
interviews with other firms,

00:10:10.330 --> 00:10:13.170
with other companies I'm
aware of several instances

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:14.550
where the partners that worked

00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:15.960
with these effected candidates

00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:17.940
tapped into their very own network

00:10:17.940 --> 00:10:19.549
trying to find some job opportunities

00:10:19.549 --> 00:10:22.100
which would be a good fit with this person

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:24.189
and then trying to have them
to get into this new role

00:10:24.189 --> 00:10:25.670
after the consulting time

00:10:25.670 --> 00:10:28.130
and then often of course,
some time of several agreement

00:10:28.130 --> 00:10:29.550
might be part of the dealers way

00:10:29.550 --> 00:10:31.510
depending on the individual circumstances.

00:10:31.510 --> 00:10:32.920
So where there are some instances

00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:35.890
where some type of legal
escalation might happen in the end

00:10:35.890 --> 00:10:38.610
these are only the rarest
cases from my experience

00:10:38.610 --> 00:10:42.150
nobody wins by doing that
especially for the tier one firms

00:10:42.150 --> 00:10:43.660
you can trust that the consulting firm

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:46.390
will do their very best to
find an amicable solution

00:10:46.390 --> 00:10:48.480
to the situation that both sides,

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:49.900
both parties can live with

00:10:49.900 --> 00:10:52.100
and of course the other
aspect of that is that

00:10:52.100 --> 00:10:54.430
because you as the effected person

00:10:54.430 --> 00:10:55.870
as the effected consultant

00:10:55.870 --> 00:10:57.946
because you know, already far in advance

00:10:57.946 --> 00:11:00.550
that you're currently on a slippery slope

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:02.980
that may be half a year,
a year down the line

00:11:02.980 --> 00:11:05.434
your future in the firm is really unclear.

00:11:05.434 --> 00:11:06.765
Most people understand

00:11:06.765 --> 00:11:08.757
that this is the track that they are on.

00:11:08.757 --> 00:11:11.675
They already by themselves
try to look around

00:11:11.675 --> 00:11:13.870
looking for other opportunities.

00:11:13.870 --> 00:11:17.940
So many people will already by
themselves have left the firm

00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:20.276
before it even gets to this former point

00:11:20.276 --> 00:11:22.789
where the HR professionals
or the responsible partner

00:11:22.789 --> 00:11:26.230
from the firm approaches
you to formally let you know

00:11:26.230 --> 00:11:28.070
that this is now the
process that you're on

00:11:28.070 --> 00:11:29.050
and you will need to leave.

00:11:29.050 --> 00:11:30.590
So, but this creates some clarity

00:11:30.590 --> 00:11:32.220
and transparency into this topic

00:11:32.220 --> 00:11:33.820
and that now you're able to understand

00:11:33.820 --> 00:11:35.540
the up-or-out principle much better

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:37.140
how it works, how it doesn't work

00:11:37.140 --> 00:11:38.310
